.SH NAME
dtkaadmin \- DTKA user function administration interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBdtkaadmin\fR [ \fIcommands_filename\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBdtkaadmin\fR configures and manages the DTKA administration database for
the local ION node, enabling the node to utilize the services of the
Trusted Collective for Delay-Tolerant Key Administration.
.PP
It configures and manages that database in response to DTKA configuration
commands found in \fIcommands_filename\fR, if provided; if not, \fBdtkaadmin\fR
prints a simple prompt (:) so that the user may type commands directly
into standard input.
.PP
The format of commands for \fIcommands_filename\fR can be queried from
\&\fBdtkaadmin\fR by entering the command 'h' or '?' at the prompt.  The
commands are documented in \fBdtkarc\fR\|(5).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
Successful completion of DTKA configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.IP dtkaadmin 4
.IX Item "dtkaadmin"
Enter interactive DTKA configuration command entry mode.
.IP "dtkaadmin host1.karc" 4
.IX Item "dtkaadmin host1.karc"
Execute all configuration commands in \fIhost1.karc\fR, then terminate
immediately.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
Status and diagnostic messages from \fBdtkaadmin\fR and from other software that
utilizes the ION node are nominally written to a log file in the current
working directory within which \fBdtkaadmin\fR was run.  The log file is
typically named \fBion.log\fR.
.PP
See also \fBdtkarc\fR\|(5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
\&\fBNote\fR: all ION administration utilities expect source file input to be
lines of ASCII text that are NL-delimited.  If you edit the dtkarc file on
a Windows machine, be sure to \fBuse dos2unix to convert it to Unix text format\fR
before presenting it to \fBdtkaadmin\fR.  Otherwise \fBdtkaadmin\fR will detect
syntax errors and will not function satisfactorily.
.PP
The following diagnostics may be issued to the log file:
.IP "Can't open command file..." 4
.IX Item "Can't open command file..."
The \fIcommands_filename\fR specified in the command line doesn't exist.
.PP
Various errors that don't cause \fBdtkaadmin\fR to fail but are noted in the
log file may be caused by improperly formatted commands given at the prompt
or in the \fIcommands_filename\fR.  Please see \fBdtkarc\fR\|(5) for details.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBdtka\fR\|(1), \fBdtkarc\fR\|(5)
